dialogue trust_redmage_3
title: Cold hands
trigger: Trust redmage level=3
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  The Red Mage has pulled a glove off to work a stubborn strap, and in the firelight the back of that hand is a map of old, shiny burn scars, laid one over another.
  * Those burns are old. Not from any fight of ours. -> old
    do: AddTrust $with 4
  * Let the Cleric see to that hand. -> cleric
    do: AddTrust $with 2
  * Say nothing, and hold the strap steady for the Red Mage. -> strap
    do: AddTrust $with 5

node old hero
  No. Not from any fight with anyone. I did these myself, a little at a time, the winter after the tithe.
  -> winter

node cleric hero
  There's nothing to see to. They healed years ago. They're only ugly, and I did them myself, the winter after the tithe.
  -> winter

node strap hero
  Thank you. You didn't ask. Most people ask. I'll tell you anyway: I did these myself, the winter after the tithe.
  -> winter

node winter hero
  My aunt's hands were cold, Commander. Always. Hollow people's hands are. So every night I'd hold them and push heat into them, the way you'd warm a pot. A little more every night. Her hands never warmed. Mine burned instead.
  -> stopped

node stopped hero
  I stopped when she asked me to. Only thing she asked for that whole winter. Not because it hurt me. Because it didn't do anything, and she could see me hoping.
  -> orb

node orb commander
  The Red Mage's eyes go to the Commander's satchel, where the orb sits wrapped.
  -> idea

node idea hero
  Here's what I keep coming back to. My fire never reached what the tithe took. But that orb wakes near you. Dead for a hundred years, and it wakes. What if fire near you could reach it too? What if it isn't heat a Hollow needs, but whatever you've got?
  -> ask

node ask commander
  The Red Mage pulls the glove back on, carefully, and waits.
  * When we next pass a Hollow who'll let us, we'll try. Together. -> promised
    do: AddTrust $with 9
    do: SetFlag redmage:test_promised
  * I don't know what I've got. I won't let you burn yourself again on a guess. -> refused
    do: AddTrust $with -3
    do: SetFlag redmage:test_refused
  * Maybe. But your aunt asked you to stop for your sake. Would she want you starting again? -> aunt_asked
    do: AddTrust $with 6
    do: SetFlag redmage:test_questioned

node promised hero
  Together. I'm writing that down somewhere in my head where I can find it. If it doesn't work, it doesn't. But I'll have tried with someone, not alone in a cold kitchen.
  -> close_line

node refused hero
  A guess is all I've ever had. You're telling me to keep my hands in my pockets and wait for someone else's answer. I've heard that before. From the Choir, mostly.
  -> close_line

node aunt_asked hero
  No. She'd want me sleeping and eating and not looking at her like a sum to solve. I don't know how to stop wanting it, though. You might have to help me with that part.
  -> close_line

node close_line hero
  The coal's still in the tin, by the way. Nine years and a season. I haven't let it go out.
  -> close

node close commander
  The Red Mage pats the coat where the tin rides, and goes back to the strap. The knot comes loose on the first pull.
